Z||000008||rogergarrison||12-31-2000||06:54 PM||||i got busted doing 60 in a 55 zone following a sheriff car for preceeding 5 miles. Hiway Patrol (fat ugly dyke type) ticketed me. When she got done, smirked that had got me, I just grinned and told her glad she did, I was doing twice that 15 minutes ago, lol. BTW I paid the whole fine in pennies.||||reg||10
Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||12-31-2000||07:45 PM||||"Shhhhh. They can hear us!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watchout.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroLisa||12-31-2000||08:13 PM||||I've used:<P>*My speedometer's broke, once I'm doing 60 it jumps all over the place (was doing 81 in 65)<BR>*Well I was going down a hill and didn't realize the momentum my car had gained!! (53 in 35)<BR>*That other car kept riding me and I had to get away from him because I was scared of him (51 in 35)<P>I have not one moving violation on my record. Ah it's good being a girl (too bad I'm not blonde anymore either) Hm I got out of an accident when I hit the car in front of me at a light with " but officer, my gas pedal stuck!" <BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||12-31-2000||08:58 PM||||A couple of times I used: "I was just enjoying the cruise and I guess I creeped up". You have to have that *sunshine smile/it's a great day to be alive* look. It worked. <P>Most of the officers I know are just glad to not have to deal with a jerk and tend to let it slide. <P>Of course, in town, you just have to bend over.....||||reg||1
Z||000012||KnightRyder31||12-31-2000||09:42 PM||||Hmmmm...<BR>" But my pizza was getting cold!!"<BR>" I guess my speedometer is messed up"<BR>" My mom is in the hospital!!!"<BR>" I have to take a pee!!!"<BR>" There is a blue Civic back there trying to kill me!!!"<BR>" A bug bit me!"<BR>" Just moving with the trafic"<BR>" I was trying to get to burger king before they start lunch!"<P>I have used all of these at least once!<BR>The " I have to pee" one really works!<P><p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||BAM-BAM||12-31-2000||09:58 PM||||  FieroLisa has a good point. Women, especially nice looking women, get out of everything. My sons girlfriend got stopped for doing 95 in a 75. The highway patrol let her slide and asked her to be a little more careful, there's alot of snow on the roads. This was in Utah. Go figure.<P> Late!!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tina||12-31-2000||10:22 PM||||Drew a blank at first, but then BF reminded me of a couple,<BR>The time PO pulled me over = Iratic Driving<BR>DL please. ....DL..??!., I don't even have my Lipstick on me.<BR>BTW would you mind turning those light's of yours off.  He did. Actually a nice guy, after I got done explaining to him that  truck had a turn radius of a about a zip-code.  <P>No Seatbelt = Just painted my nails,hate to get them all messed up. <P>Lay on that german/french or whatever accent really thick.<P>The last one was pure concidence. <BR>Already pulled over,Cell rings, a friend calling. ME to PO " Can you hold please"<BR>He just started laughing.<BR>  <BR>Tina<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||firstfiero||12-31-2000||11:57 PM||||   sure fire way for me to get out of a ticket is tell them my uncle is the mayor. It's true and I've gotten out of tickets because of it.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> 86se||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroLisa||01-01-2001||01:49 AM||||Tina- I got pulled over the other day when driving my mother's 1988 econoline van (it is THE largest piece of crap vehicle in the US), it had no taillights. Cop comes up and asks for my drivers license, but I was just headed to the gym and didn't have it. But for some stupid reason, I knew my license nubmber off the top of my head and the guy was pretty impressed with that. First time I acted smart to get out of a ticket!!! (and YES i act smart the rest of the time for those of you who were going to make fun of me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I also got pulled over for "drunk driving" (ha, I had just gotten off work) when I was just reaching to shut my cell phone ringer off! Cop was a real d*ck, he was all like "well I could give you a reckless driving ticket for that, your pretty lucky young lady"<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000017||turbo86se||01-01-2001||03:30 AM||||Funniest excuse I ever heard was when I was riding with my good friend, a county policeman, we stopped a guy for speeding, and failure to stop. His excuse was, "my wife just left me for a county policeman, and I thought you were trying to give her back!" I've never seen him laugh that hard!!  LOL||||reg||1
Z||000018||firstfiero||01-01-2001||10:40 AM||||    I know how that is fierolisa...I got pulled over last January at 2 in the morning on freezing cold night because the police officer said one of my 2 license plate lights were out. He needs to be able to see my license number from 50 ft away and he couldn't from any more then 40. That was lambest exscuse to look for a dui I ever saw.  You don't even want to get me started on the legality of sobriety check points!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> 86se||||reg||1
Z||000019||TheFiero64||01-01-2001||11:37 AM||||Last summer there were 3 of us heading to meet the rest of our convoy on the way to a Fiero show. Gokart was in the lead I was in the middle and GTSONLY was in the back. We pulled out of a gas station squealing the rubber. Not noticing there was a cop parked in the same lot we just pulled from. I looked back and saw the flashing lights and noticed we were up to 50 already in a 35. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> We all stopped and the cop said "What do you think this is the Indy 500" I felt like telling him that the 84 Fiero paced at indy but I decided not to push my luck. Gokart said Were sorry but we were late to meet our friends up the street. The cop said "I don't care who your gonna go meet slow it down." He also said "How dumb do you think I am its bad enough to have pulled over one of you but to have 3 of you speeding by me makes it look really stupid" He let us go and we drove nice and slow then when we met the others we told the story and had a hysterical laugh.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000020||82-T/A||01-01-2001||11:49 AM||||In my less mature days, I was busted once for doing over 120 miles an hour, and another time doing probably around 110-115 miles an hour. <P>THe 120 was on this long stretch of road that goes by an industrial park.. very little traffic even during rush hour. <P>I was hauling ass, probably doing about 125.. the Fiero was at it's peak.. like 5,500 rpms.. and it couldn't pull anymore (top speed is calculated by power = coefficient of drag x gearing / torque)<BR>and the needle was pegged at 120 and had been.. so I guess it didn't have enough HP to get it going a little quicker. <P>Anyway, I flew past the oNLY car on the entire road, an all black Dodge Stratus with black tinted windows... who would have thought it was a cop. <P>He pulled me over.. by using his siren. He was dressed up like someone from Hawaii 5-0 or something. He had bermuda shorts and a hawaiian shirt on. I'm guessing he was undercover narcotics or something. But he let me go, he told me to calm down and not speed. <P><BR>The other time, I was hauling ass down a long stretch of road in my 85 GT.. had the tack pegged.. I think my top speed was like 115 cause it had 4.10s in it. The speedo was busted. I think I flew by the cop soo fast, that he didn't even have time to clock me. But he pulled me over and was extremely pissed at me. I gave him my liscense and registration. About 2 minutes later, he ran up to my car, THREW the stuff at me and said.. "Consider yourself lucky." he got back in his cop car and peeled out of there with his sirens on. Guess he had more important things to do.<P>I haven't been pulled over in almost two years now.. heh... oh well.. actually... I was pulled over in Daytona 2000 for doing 10 miles over the speedlimit..<P>APPARENTLY.. one of you other guys in a medium metallic red Fiero was doing a burnout out of the Holiday Inn, and I got busted for it...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000021||Greg Piet||01-01-2001||02:21 PM||||You are the one who got nailed for that holiday inn fiasco???????   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Normally I take my medicine.  If I get pulled over, I answer the questions honestly, and be very polite, keep my hands on the steering wheel.  EXCEPT ONCE where I got pulled over for going 45 in a 25(speedtrap around New London, Wisconsin) but I was not in the 25 zone yet even after I pulled over.  I remained as polite as possible and told the cop that the last speed limit sign was 300 yards back, and it says 45.  When he called me a liar I lost it...  I thought I was going to jail, but he let me go by some miracle.||||reg||1
Z||000022||rogergarrison||01-01-2001||02:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BAM-BAM:<BR><B>  FieroLisa has a good point. Women, especially nice looking women, get out of everything. My sons girlfriend got stopped for doing 95 in a 75. The highway patrol let her slide and asked her to be a little more careful, there's alot of snow on the roads. This was in Utah. Go figure.<P> Late!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>AMEN TO THAT BAM, LOL<P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||82-T/A||01-01-2001||04:26 PM||||Heheh.. yeah, it was kind of emberassing too because they announced it at the banquet dinner too... they said, "Someone in the medium metallic red Fiero coupe already was busted, so everyone watch out for speed traps!"<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000024||Lisa 86 2m4||01-01-2001||07:29 PM||||The few times I've been pulled over, and am still ticketless, I always go with the "But officer, I never speed! The speed limit here is-- and I would never go faster than that!" Which usually is responded with a "Well, miss, maybe  your speedometer is broken." and I can't help but to ham up a bit with "YOu mean a speedometer can break?" Yeah, well, I'm blonde, too so that really does help.  But I've been pulled over three times for having a neon pink license plate cover,too! Then they usually check over the car and tell me it's illegal, again, I just play dumb and say "but it's been on my car for almost -- years" I think those are just bored cops. ||||reg||1
Z||000025||gtsonly||01-02-2001||07:19 PM||||The Rutland 2000 show, Three of us went tearing out of a gas station right in front of a cop. Needless to say, he yanked all of us over, told us to slow down but let us go ticket free.<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||6
Z||000026||stomper282||01-02-2001||10:35 PM||||The last time I was pulled over I aske the cop "Are you selling tickets to the police mans ball??" He repiled "police men dont have balls!" Needless to say I got a ticket<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000027||jerpro||01-03-2001||12:05 AM||||well... the key to get out of tickets it to get the cop off track and say whatever bs you can think of. just make him smile.<BR>My last encounter, 85 on a 45. <BR>I was pulled over and while he was writing the ticket I asked him if he was going to take that ticket to john clark (he is the sheriff at my area) he looked at me amazed and asked me how is it that I knew him. <BR>We talked for a couple minutes like normal people (ha!) and then he simply let me go without a waring or anything. (actually I told him I had to go and he said have a good day)<BR>It was wierd but hey!!! it worked!!<BR>Another time I was pulled over and I started shaking and dropping everything. I keep the registration behind the passenger seat so I got out of the car and went around to get it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I was making such a scene that he simply looked at my lisense gave it back to me and told me to go home and rest.<BR>oh well, I just might be very lucky but hey!! Life is supposed to be fun!!<BR>If I ever get the guts I will do the bee scene from the movie tommy boy. Hopefully it works  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000028||rodmcneill||01-03-2001||12:26 AM||||Hey Jerpro, I liked when you told the cop that you had to go, that was classic! All this talk about getting pulled over reminds me of the Cheech and Chong movie, Up In Smoke. When the motorcycle cop pulls them over, by the time he has inhaled some of the "smoke" coming from there truck he forgets why he stopped them!||||reg||12
Z||000029||80's BOY||01-03-2001||07:00 PM||||or you could bore them to death with Fiero information. i got pulled over the other night just cruising.....78 in a 65....i had just change out my 85 gauges with backlit 87 gauges. when i got pulled over, i started explaining intelligently about the differences in the two sets of guages, and how much nicer the backlit guages were. also about how the Fiero was discontinued...blah blah blah... i didn't get a ticket, he just wanted me to leave!!!||||reg||1
Z||000030||jerpro||01-03-2001||08:30 PM||||hey my first post no. 30!! hehehe!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I also t boned into a bmw with rusted old caravan.<BR>My fault but no ticket. HE was going WAAAAY over the speed limit.<BR>ahhh am I kucky  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000031||jerpro||01-03-2001||11:00 PM||||?!??!?!!?!?! the book did not go on flames??<P><BR>------------------------------------------------<BR>ahh now it did....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by jerpro (edited 01-03-2001).]||||reg||1
