Z||000033||Raydar||01-04-2001||09:41 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rodmcneill:<BR><B>...the Cheech and Chong movie, Up In Smoke. When the motorcycle cop pulls them over</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>And another scene...<P>"Could I see your license?"<P>"Uhhh..." &lt;pointing towards rear of car&gt; "It's back there on the bumper!"<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000034||cowans||01-04-2001||11:46 AM||||Here's a good one...I will prefix it by saying I'm an ex/ Montreal, Quebec boy and you need a good French H'ac-cent to fully enjoy. I will try and add consonants where necessary!!!<BR>My friend is driving down Decarie Expressway(Mtl) and gets pulled over by the 'Securite de Police'. The officer approches the car and requests,  "License et Enregistriment" (drivers license & registration). The constable simply states "Wait two minute, I, be back" in brok'en h'Eng-lish. Friend waits... All of a sudden, both constables jump from their car, run back, and one states, (again in brok'en h'Eng-lish), "It says on your Li-cense, you 'ave a restriction "D", it mean you're to were glasses while driving!!". My friend states " Yes, but I have "contacts""!! The officer thinks, then replies angrily... "I don't care Who You Know, you're to wear glasses while driving." Oh! To be a Quebec'r again....<BR>you'd 'ave to be th-ere'<BR>thanks for the memory, Sandy||||reg||10
Z||000035||TheFiero64||01-04-2001||12:07 PM||||LMAO Racer 1,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/laugh2.gif"> <BR>I have to use that Firestone excuse. I wonder if the cop would look to see that I have Michelin Pilots on my rims.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That made my day thanks,<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000036||kevin||01-04-2001||04:56 PM||||Next time your stopped, do what I do and request the violation be heard ( this is assuming all the above excuses do not work), in the count seat. The cops are required to accept your request. Oftentimes, the county seat is too far away for them to show up as the prosecution witness. If they do not show up during arraignment, you walk. It worked for me! ||||reg||1
Z||000037||kinboyatuwo||01-05-2001||12:58 PM||||Got cought racing and said i was trying to warn the car that he had a flame under the car and he thought i was racing and kept going faster<BR>the cop said ya right<BR>i said thats the only reason i was behind him<P><BR>hee hee, he said thanks and laughed and no ticket<BR><P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||4
Z||000038||Raydar||01-05-2001||03:28 PM||||A while back, I knew a guy who got pulled over (actually knew MANY people who got pulled over). He got out of his car, took out his wallet, and stood by the door as the officer approached him, with ticket book in hand. He raised his wallet to his mouth, opened it, and said "Beam me up, Scotty! NOW!" <BR>Officer laughed and let him go with a warning. <BR>This was a long time ago, before everyone started saying it. I think the original series was still on TV. ||||reg||1
Z||000039||Tigger||01-08-2001||07:19 PM||||Well you see, the guy ahead of me threw his cigarette out the window and I tried to step on it.||||reg||3
